From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:07:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: offload Wi-Fi NPU flows in the PPE

A flow to a Wi-Fi station behind the NPU never bound in the PPE.
The driver waits for the transmit path to complete an entry, and no
QDMA transmit runs for a frame that the NPU sends. A Wi-Fi flow
without a flowtable rule had no bind path, and no event removed a
Wi-Fi flow when its interface went away.

A flow to or from a Wi-Fi station now binds, with or without a
flowtable rule. mt76 reports each frame that it hands to the NPU
through a new PPE device operation, and the receive operation takes
the CPU reason. Both change the public header, so mt76 must carry
the matching change. The DSCP of a Wi-Fi entry holds 6 bits, because
the NPU selects the WMM queue from it. When a Wi-Fi interface goes
down or away, the driver deletes the conntrack entries of all routed
Wi-Fi flows.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
